When Nethack is looking for a letter to answer a prompt, it will often
accept a space for the normal response.  But with a tin, this should not
be done, because there isn't a proper normal response.  I find that I
lose half my spinach due to pressing the space bar.

It is not so easy to open this tin.--more--
The dog hits the grid bug.  The grid bug is killed!--more--
You hear someone counting money.--more--
(several more messages)
It smells like spinach.  Eat it? (oops, one space too many)
You discard the open tin.

The default shouldn't be the other way, either; just substitute
cockatrices for spinach and you can see why.  Instead, a space bar
should not be accepted here.


